---
description: Definition of done — applies when building or reviewing a screen
globs: ["src/features/**", "src/patterns/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Done means all three columns pass, not just the first.

## 1 · Mechanical — `npm run verify`

self-test · contrast · tokens · provenance · i18n · types · lint · tests · trace.
Run it before you claim anything. The `afterFileEdit` hook runs a subset on
every edit; it is not a substitute for the full gate.

## 2 · Requirement

- Every FR in the screen's `satisfies` list is **implemented, not stubbed**
- `@requirement FR-xx` in the file header, and `npm run trace` counts it
- Anything marked `MOCKED` / `SIMULATED` is a **convincing, visibly labelled
  simulation** — not a TODO, not a real integration

## 3 · Judgement — what no tool can check

- [ ] **All four data states exist** — `loading` skeletons matching the final
      layout, `empty` offering the action that creates the first item, `error`
      with a retry, `noData` as grey with a last-seen time. Not four variations
      on a spinner. Use the `DataStateProps` union; it makes the wrong shape
      unconstructible.
- [ ] **Switch to Indonesian and look at it.** Strings run 20–30 % longer. Every
      truncation and wrap bug lives here and no tool will find it.
- [ ] **375 px and 200 % zoom** — no horizontal scroll at either.
- [ ] **Tab through the whole screen.** Every stop visible, every action
      reachable.
- [ ] Does it open on **the decision its role owns**, or on a wall of data?
- [ ] One primary action per area.
- [ ] No dead ends — every alert and every severity leads somewhere.

## What done is not

- ✗ "It renders." A screen that is green everywhere demonstrates nothing — the
  unhappy paths are the product. Offline units, stale readings, absent sensors,
  failed commands and a restricted unit all need to be visible in the demo.
- ✗ "Verify passes." Verify proves you did not break the rules. It cannot tell
  you the screen answers the question its role opens on.
- ✗ "I'll add provenance / empty states / Indonesian later." Each is a full
  second pass over every screen. That is exactly why they are gated from the
  first commit rather than the last.
